    {
      "description": "## Duplicate watcher proof\n\nA server snapshot can count connected daemon keys by environment, but it cannot prove the singleton process invariant: snapshots are keyed by `machine_id:env_name`, so a second daemon can replace/collapse the first. **Duplicate watcher count is not measurable from current server telemetry.** Do not read a displayed `1` as proof of one process.\n\nFor an activity-card incident, compare same-epoch stage counts in path order: extracted → queued → sent → acked → server accepted → server broadcast → browser converted → browser rendered. They show stage loss, but are not a correlated per-card trace.",
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": {}, "overrides": [] },
